{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788374949,"nonce":"UdqJDtreO4yOt9jk4I3mmusRQQ0=","message":"Second occurrence of this issue's third acceptance clause, same day, different verb — `bill-set`.\n\n    bill-set {bench:11825, uid:\"Bill_...\", target_count:500}\n      -\u003e ok:true, data:{}            (nothing changed; target stayed 10)\n      -\u003e journal warning: unknown arg 'target_count' ... DROPPED and the verb\n         RAN ANYWAY\n\nThe arg is spelled `target`, not `target_count` — and `target_count` is\nexactly what `bills` PUBLISHES the field as, so the round-trip name does not\nmatch the write name. With `target` the same call returns a populated\n`targets[].changed` list:\n\n    changed: [{field:'target', value:500}, {field:'unpause_when_you_have', value:495}]\n\nSo the honest signal exists — `data` is EMPTY on the dropped-arg call and\npopulated on the real one — but the verdict is `ok:true` either way, and a\ncaller that branches on `ok` (which is what the protocol asks callers to do)\ncannot tell them apart. Same as the `landmark` case above: `ok:true` with an\nempty result on a MUTATING verb.\n\nTwo occurrences, two different verbs, so per `checklists/README.md`\n§The promotion pass this is promote-or-reject rather than a one-off. Proposed\nrule, cheap and general: **if a mutating verb dropped EVERY argument that\nwould have made it mutate, the verdict is `refused` with the unknown-arg list\nas `error.detail`, not `ok`.** The unknown-arg tracker that writes the journal\nwarning already knows everything needed to decide this.\n\nRead-only verbs keep the current behaviour — `things` dropping `near`/`radius`\nand answering map-wide is a warning-worthy surprise but not a lie about a\nmutation that did not happen.\n\nAlso worth naming while it is in front of us: `bill-add`'s `count` is NOT the\ntarget count (it left the bill at the default 10 and reported success), which\nis the same trap one verb earlier in the same workflow.","files":null}]}